WEBVTT

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.460
You don't look so happy, Kasuga-san.

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:10.630
You don't understand
the situation you're in, do you?

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:11.930
Don't give me that.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.400
You're the one that spurred me on
to go to Karasumori.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:19.550
But then, I thought you would last longer
than one night

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.070
after I told you about it.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:28.550
Hmm... It looks like it'll be
a pain to deal with.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:32.490
All right, Yoshimori. Let's see how
you'll take care of this one.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:33.850
He's...

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.330
That's too bad for you.

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:39.790
Ketsu!

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:41.260
Metsu!

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.170
Mas-san.
When did you get back?

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:52.010
What are you doing here?!

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:54.310
Well, can you blame me for worrying
about my brother

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:55.340
who does so poorly?

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:00.950
You haven't improved much over
the last three years, have you?

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:08.800
The dangerous forest invites me
It's showtime again tonight

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.670
(Ayakashi NIGHT)

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:15.870
Everyone's rampaging
with all their strength

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:17.770
(Fighting late into the night)

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:21.210
Drive away all hesitation

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:25.610
Wanna take them on? Yeah

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:29.150
I will protect you
(No matter what)

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:32.490
I will protect you that's all
(that's all I want)

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:38.150
Goodbye to the days
when all I'd do was cry

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:42.660
Sha la la la la...

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:49.070
I hold words in my heart
that I'd like to say

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:51.040
(Secret romance)

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:56.240
Standing in front of me is someone
I don't want to lose

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.010
(A strange distance)

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:04.850
I can't stand watching
people get hurt anymore

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:05.920
Yeah

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.390
I wanna be your knight
(I wanna be strong)

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:12.990
I wanna be your light
(More than I am now)

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:18.330
Someday I'll share with you
my 100% smile

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:38.650
That's odd.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.620
We're in the middle of class

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:43.180
and Sumimura-kun isn't asleep.

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:47.460
I wonder if it has something
to do with ghosts.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.730
So about that dumpling place...

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:55.760
Hey! Yuri is...

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:59.500
It must be love!
You can't stop it once it gets rolling!

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:04.310
I heard that your older brother
is back for a visit?

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.440
You mean that
really cool-looking older brother?

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:11.410
So what's your older brother like,
Sumimura-kun?

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.610
Shut up!

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:15.850
What?!

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:17.720
Looks like she got turned down.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.320
I don't get those two.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.190
What's wrong?

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:24.760
He's not cool at all!

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:43.080
Whether you live or die...
is all up to you Yoshimori.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:46.710
I'm home!

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:49.380
Yoshimori.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:55.350
What?

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:59.570
Grandfather was lamenting about
your mischievousness.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.100
I heard you released
Madarao's seal.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:05.970
Make it quick.
I want to take a nap.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:07.000
There. There.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.570
By the way, don't you think
Tokine-chan's grown up

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:11.940
to be really beautiful?

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:13.900
Really?

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:16.110
What's with him?

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:18.840
Back in the day...

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.920
...we used to play with
each other. Remember?

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:26.020
We had snowball fights.

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:32.560
We flew kites together.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:40.540
Hard to believe
she's the same girl.

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:46.670
Damn it you don't know anything
about how I feel.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.310
So. About Tokine-chan.

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:53.140
Do you still like her?

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.160
You're devoted to her.
Aren't you?

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.210
Here's some tissue.

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:03.900
Tokine-chan is two years older
than you, right?

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.050
You like older women?

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.960
I hate this guy!

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.070
Let's get to the main issue.

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:14.030
As usual, you're relying on force
when you fight.

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:15.400
Are you lecturing me?

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:16.430
Yes, I'm lecturing you.

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:21.340
Listen. Yoshimori.
You have to think before you act.

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:24.150
Are you aware of the advantage the ones

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:25.310
who have their sights
on Karasumori have?

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:31.920
They can increase their power with
Karasumori's power, right?

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:35.720
That's one of them. But there's another.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:38.370
They have one
large advantage over you.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.990
We don't know their identity.

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:45.940
We don't know what kind of Ayakashi
will come next.

00:05:45.970 --> 00:05:48.030
What they look like, how they're shaped
or what powers they will have.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.180
There's no way to know that.

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:53.940
But you can assume that information
about us has been leaked to them.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:58.050
That's why you have to think
before you act.

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.020
It doesn't always
go the way you want it

00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:01.210
just because you think ahead.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:04.120
But it'll help you make
better decisions when fighting.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:06.830
You're too naïve.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.860
If I was an enemy after Karasumori...

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:15.670
It would only take me one night to
conquer that castle.

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:26.310
You still haven't mastered
the Kekkai techniques, have you?

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:30.850
The techniques can be very versatile.
For example...

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:44.960
Even just designating the targets
to surround like that

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.230
should give you more options.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:50.930
You can't beat Tokine-chan

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:52.870
in terms of how you think
and in your use of the techniques.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:56.370
I don't care about
who wins or loses.

00:06:57.610 --> 00:06:59.670
I don't understand
the complicated stuff.

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:02.880
As long as there's no disasters...

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:06.890
As long as no one gets hurt.
I'm fine with that...

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:11.830
You're very kind.
But much too naïve.

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:15.790
I'm telling you
to think about things logically

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:18.760
because there are
many things in this world

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:20.830
that can't be dealt with
by just using emotions.

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:25.170
Do you still not understand
the responsibility of this work?

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:29.310
It's not just about the site or the areas
around the school. Or this town.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:30.710
It's more than that.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:33.270
You are responsible for
the lives of all mankind.

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.310
Hurry up and get it
through your head.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:38.550
You are the Legitimate Heir.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:42.250
Don't think you can run away
from that responsibility

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:43.760
by saying naïve things like that.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.760
What's his problem?!

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:57.670
"It would only take me one night
to conquer that castle."

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:00.740
What are you?
You from the Sengoku era?!

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:08.450
The Legitimate Heir, huh?

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:24.100
Impressive!

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:29.140
This is quite a feast!

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:34.210
Well, Masamori suddenly came back,
so I went all out.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:37.340
Oh? I thought I sent
you an e-mail?

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:38.570
You did?!

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:41.370
Sorry, I haven't touched
my computer in a while.

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:43.010
Com... puter?

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:44.580
You should buy a cell phone.

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:45.640
Cell... phone?

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:47.380
But I'll never use it.

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:48.480
They're convenient to have.

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:52.590
If you're a Caster,
use your Shikigami!

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:55.260
But it's faster this way.

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:57.500
- The dinner table always seems...
- What's this e-mail you're talking about?!

00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:58.530
- So cramped when he's back.
- Would you like to try it?

00:08:58.530 --> 00:08:59.860
You should, Grandpa.

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:02.470
Can I move over to there?

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:04.400
Siblings must eat side-by-side!

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:08.530
I'm sleepy...

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:12.470
I didn't get a good nap
because of my stupid brother.

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:19.020
I don't get it.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.660
What's the meaning of
this thing anyway?

00:09:26.590 --> 00:09:27.650
I'm off!

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:30.020
Be careful.

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:37.970
You look like
you're in a bad mood.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:40.300
But I don't blame you.

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:41.330
Yoshimori!

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:45.240
Isn't Masamori-san coming
with us today?

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:47.740
Shut up!

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:48.440
- Huh?
- Huh?

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:49.510
How should I know?!

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:52.480
The Legitimate Heir?
I don't care about that!

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:55.510
I'm only fighting so Tokine
will never get hurt again!

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:56.850
That's enough for me!

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:01.860
I don't like that man.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.490
It's here! Let's go!

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:16.370
Hey, there's nothing here.

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:21.340
That's odd. I'm sure the scent
is coming from around here.

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:23.610
But...

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:42.100
W-What is this?!

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:49.640
Before long, this forest will
swallow up all of the school.

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:55.510
Let's see what you've got, Yoshimori.

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:01.110
Is this...

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:06.280
...a forest?

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:13.120
Let's see what you got Yoshimori.

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:14.830
I want to see your powers

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:17.360
as well as the current power
of Karasumori.

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:20.400
Madarao. Is this some kind
of Ayakashi too?

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:23.840
Yeah. It's unusual.
It's a botanical Ayakashi.

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:27.040
Botanical ones
have no will of their own...

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:31.080
Unless someone set it up here
they wouldn't appear in a place like this.

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:34.490
I don't get it, damn it!

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:35.680
Ketsu!

00:11:37.390 --> 00:11:38.050
Metsu!

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:44.090
As expected from a tree!

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:45.720
They don't move,
so this will be easy!

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:53.270
Oh, how big...

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:55.900
Why, you...

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:56.930
Wait!

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:00.880
Stop wasting your strength!

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:03.910
We have to look into what this...
forest is.

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:06.720
But did you see
how fast it's growing?

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:10.190
It'll continue to grow
if we don't hurry. See?

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:17.220
But destroying everything
we see won't be enough.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:19.130
Think of a better tactic!

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:24.100
You have to think
before you act.

00:12:25.670 --> 00:12:27.640
She's saying
the same thing he did!

00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:29.570
Ketsu!

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:30.270
Hey!

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:31.100
Metsu!

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:33.080
I said stop!

00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:35.550
That's useless.

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:38.510
The greatest power of the forest
I planted here...

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:41.390
is its ability to proliferate!

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:48.960
You better think a little...
or else the forest will continue to grow.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.230
Anyways we have to
stop it from growing.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:54.900
If I can just figure out
how it works...

00:12:59.040 --> 00:12:59.700
Metsu!

00:13:01.310 --> 00:13:04.540
Hey! What do you think
you're doing, honey?

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.780
Oh my god!

00:13:11.550 --> 00:13:12.540
I see.

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:14.110
Look.

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:18.760
The base regenerated,
but the cut portion doesn't.

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:23.360
So you're saying we need
to crush the roots.

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:26.160
But I don't know how far
the roots go down.

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:27.030
SCHOOL
ANTI-AYAKASHI
KEKKAI
SHRINE
KEKKAI

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:31.910
SCHOOL
ANTI-AYAKASHI
KEKKAI
SHRINE
KEKKAI
Grandma has said that there is
a powerful Kekkai around the shrine.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:35.040
SCHOOL
ANTI-AYAKASHI
KEKKAI
SHRINE
KEKKAI
And the Ayakashi can't go
down past one meter.

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:37.940
So the roots shouldn't be that deep.

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:42.210
You're right.
But that's not entirely accurate.

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:45.750
The Kekkai doesn't prevent
the Ayakashi from going deeper.

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:49.420
When Ayakashi go too close
to Karasumori.

00:13:49.420 --> 00:13:51.580
They're devoured by Karasumori.

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:54.380
Tokine!

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:58.260
I found something
amazing over there.

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:05.400
The best way to deal with
these trees is to aim for the center.

00:14:06.270 --> 00:14:08.470
From the outside
it may look like a forest

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:10.370
but it's actually a single tree.

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:14.480
Originally it was nothing
but a regular tree seed

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:16.610
with a parasitic botanical
Ayakashi attached.

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:18.490
I placed a talisman

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:20.110
that increased its rate of growth.

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:22.380
Destroy that part
and you can stop the growth.

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:26.920
But the power of Karasumori
is unpredictable.

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:29.530
Look at how much
it has grown already.

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:33.130
How will it evolve next?

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:36.960
Honey?

00:14:37.840 --> 00:14:40.570
I've been looking for the root,

00:14:40.610 --> 00:14:45.070
but the Ayakashi
at the core is moving.

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:46.810
This is going to be a problem.

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:51.440
What's wrong?

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:52.950
See? Look at that.

00:14:57.760 --> 00:14:59.090
Ew, it's moving!

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:00.760
Doesn't it look bad?

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:02.490
Yoshimori! That thing is dangerous!

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:06.660
I can smell a very strong poison
coming from it

00:15:06.700 --> 00:15:08.760
and an aura different from the tree.

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:11.600
And it's getting stronger.

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:13.830
This is bad!

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:18.530
Ketsu!

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:28.380
That was close.

00:15:30.460 --> 00:15:31.450
Yoshimori!

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:41.260
Metsu!

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:49.770
Come with me. Tokine!

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:53.680
Yoshimori, we have to call for backup!

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:56.180
There's too much
we don't know about this.

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:58.880
Masamori-san is back. So...

00:15:58.920 --> 00:15:59.910
No way!

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:03.520
I'm not asking him for help!

00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:05.190
I don't want to either.

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:08.290
You idiot!
Why are you being stubborn?

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:12.300
She's right. I don't like him,
but Mas-san is strong.

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:13.960
Geez! Shut up!

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:15.460
I'll do something about it!

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:17.690
Okay, but what
are you going to do?

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:19.770
I'll surround this entire forest!

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:22.870
How much power
do you think you'll need

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:24.710
to destroy
something this huge?!

00:16:25.050 --> 00:16:28.480
I don't know if I can destroy it...

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:33.150
...but I'm pretty sure
I can surround the whole thing.

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:35.320
What are you going to do after that?

00:16:36.190 --> 00:16:38.850
Hey... I thought about this...

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:40.820
But can't you burn it?

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:42.860
I'm sure you can burn it.

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:45.030
Well. Its basic structure is of a tree.

00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:50.070
Right? Maybe we can do that...
I saw it somewhere...

00:16:50.240 --> 00:16:55.440
What do you call that?
Um... Ba... Ba...

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:04.950
Don't be silly.
Are you sure you can do it?

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:05.940
Yeah.

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:07.840
I can.

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:13.450
All right. I'll help.

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:18.960
I don't think you should do it, honey.

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:22.840
It'll be more dangerous
if we leave it all to Yoshimori.

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:31.340
It's evolving more than I expected!

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:33.680
I'll have to stop it soon... Huh?!

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:42.280
Th-That idiot!
Is he trying to surround everything?!

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:50.460
Ketsu!

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:56.700
The size is impressive but...

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:00.430
it's unstable.

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:03.510
He won't be able to destroy it
in that state.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:08.310
You have to stabilize it.

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:10.510
Shut up! Don't talk!

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:12.350
Listen Yoshimori.

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:15.210
It's up to you to make
this plan work.

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.720
No matter what happens
focus on building your Kekkai.

00:18:19.560 --> 00:18:21.550
I'll set fire to the forest.

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:24.790
So they're going to burn it.
How foolish.

00:18:25.300 --> 00:18:27.270
The burn won't keep pace
with the tree's growth.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:33.770
Once the fire uses up all
the oxygen inside the Kekkai

00:18:33.810 --> 00:18:34.800
it'll be my turn.

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:38.400
Yoshimori! Can you do it?!

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:40.340
Okay!

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:43.210
Ketsu!

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:45.340
Metsu!

00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:56.430
Once the smoldering fire
gains oxygen...

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:58.360
It will burn up in an instant!

00:18:58.800 --> 00:18:59.790
And then!

00:19:01.340 --> 00:19:02.320
Oh no!

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:03.700
- It'll explode!
- It'll explode!

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:14.010
A back draft phenomenon!

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:19.440
I didn't think
they would make it explode.

00:19:19.990 --> 00:19:23.790
Thanks to the Kekkai around the school
no one can hear it.

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:26.030
But they're too reckless.

00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:33.520
Will it really burn through everything?

00:19:34.030 --> 00:19:36.160
That's all up to Yoshi.

00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:39.140
Good luck Yoshimori.

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:41.840
Don't lose focus!

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:44.400
You have to concentrate!

00:19:44.610 --> 00:19:46.370
This was your idea!

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:51.120
You're putting too much force
into it!

00:19:56.490 --> 00:19:58.520
Oh. No!
It won't last any longer!

00:19:58.690 --> 00:20:00.130
Get back. Hakubi!

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:04.090
Tenketsu!

00:20:12.070 --> 00:20:13.230
Damn it!

00:20:14.510 --> 00:20:15.600
Tenketsu!

00:20:54.650 --> 00:20:57.480
It looks like we defeated it somehow...

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:00.650
but this is going to be a huge pain
to clean up.

00:21:05.260 --> 00:21:06.320
I'm going to call for backup!

00:21:07.090 --> 00:21:08.820
You're not going to stop me this time.

00:21:23.110 --> 00:21:26.080
I helped him only because
of that look on his face...

00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:30.850
but I never thought he'd be able
to pull off such a crazy idea.

00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:35.220
You fool!

00:21:35.790 --> 00:21:38.220
What did you do to make
such a huge mess?!

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:41.460
Shut up!
I didn't have a choice!

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:44.690
Like grandfather like grandson.

00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:48.440
How about we
clean this up quickly?

00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:51.340
This happened because
of your incompetent grandson.

00:21:51.470 --> 00:21:52.730
What did you say?!

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:55.970
Your super useless granddaughter
helped out too!

00:21:56.080 --> 00:21:58.010
- What did you say, geezer?
- Oh, you guys.

00:21:58.150 --> 00:22:00.510
You really are crazy.

00:22:03.580 --> 00:22:06.480
How long do you think you can keep up
this way of doing things?

00:22:14.290 --> 00:22:15.850
I don't believe it.

00:22:16.500 --> 00:22:20.090
After creating such a huge Kekkai
he doesn't even look tired.

00:22:21.570 --> 00:22:24.200
He just isn't able to control it yet...

00:22:24.970 --> 00:22:27.840
...the overabundant strength inside him.

00:22:38.390 --> 00:22:46.090
The breeze blows past us
in this city we know so well

00:22:46.090 --> 00:22:52.790
The two of us both walk at our usual pace

00:22:54.370 --> 00:23:02.180
Joking around I noticed after I laughed

00:23:02.180 --> 00:23:08.510
Your mature look that
I had never seen before

00:23:10.450 --> 00:23:18.360
You don't have to say anything it's okay

00:23:19.660 --> 00:23:24.720
I'm not mistaking these feelings

00:23:26.300 --> 00:23:33.810
Straight ahead I'm pushing forward

00:23:33.810 --> 00:23:41.340
Yet I can't help but keep gazing at you

00:23:43.080 --> 00:23:50.320
Even if we are near or far

00:23:50.320 --> 00:23:58.890
The red string connects one to another
